t/download/table/ins820721/Table 3/yoda.h5","yoda1":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 3/yoda1"},"description":"Correlations coefficients of the unfolded asymmetries.","doi":"10.17182/hepdata.55300.v1/t3","id":48309,"location":"Data from T 4,F 5","messages":false,"name":"Table 3","processed_name":"Table3","resources":[]},{"data":{"csv":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/csv","json":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/json","root":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/root","yaml":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/yaml","yoda":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/yoda","yoda.h5":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/yoda.h5","yoda1":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins820721/Table 4/yoda1"},"description":"The measured strange quark helicity distribution as a funxtion of X.","doi":"10.17182/hepdata.55300.v1/t4","id":48311,"location":"Data from F7","messages":false,"name":"Table 4","processed_name":"Table4","resources":[]}],"mode":"record","overall_status":"finished","participant_count":0,"recid":55300,"record":{"abstract":"We present a LO evaluation of helicity densities of valence, \\Delta u_v+\\Delta d_v, non-strange sea, \\Delta\\bar{u}+\\Delta\\bar{d}, and strange quarks, \\Delta s (assumed to be equal to \\Delta\\bar{s}). They have been obtained from the inclusive asymmetry A_{3,d} and the semi-inclusive asymmetries A^{\\pi+}_{1,d}, A^{\\pi-}_{1,d}, A^{K+}_{1,d}, A^{K-}_{1,d} measured in polarised deep inelastic muon-deuteron scattering. The full deuteron statistics of COMPASS (years 2002-2004 and 2006) has been used. The data cover the range Q^2 > 1 (GeV/c)^2 and 0.004<x<0.3. Both non-strange densities are found to be in a good agreement with previous measurements. The distribution of \\Delta s(x) is compatible with zero in the whole measured range, in contrast to the shape of the strange quark helicity distribution obtained in most LO and NLO QCD fits. The sensitivity of the values of \\Delta s(x) upon the choice of fragmentation functions used in the derivation is discussed.","access_urls":{"links":{"csv":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins820721/1/csv","json":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins820721/1/json","root":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins820721/1/root","yaml":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins820721/1/yaml","yoda":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins820721/1/yoda"}},"analyses":[],"arxiv_id":"arXiv:0905.2828","collaborations":["COMPASS"],"control_number":"55300","creation_date":"2009-05-01","data_abstract":"CERN-SPS. Measurement of the spin asymmetries and quark helicity densities in inclusive and semi-inclusive (charged pion and kaon)  muon deuteron  interactions with incident beam momenta from 140 to 180 GeV. The full COMPASS  deuteron statistics from the years 2002-2004 and 2006 are used covering the Q**2  range &gt; 1 GeV**2 and X from 0.004 to 0.3.  The experiment uses a longitudinally polarised deuterated lithium target in which alternate cells are polarised in  opposite directions so that data from both spin directions can be recorded at the same time and a longitudinally polarized muon beam with energy constrained to be between 140 and 180 GeV.  The asymmetry in cross sections  between parallel,   S1=Z,S2=Z,and anti-parallel, S1=Z,S2=-Z, spin data is measured.     Numerical values supplied by G Mallott.","data_keywords":{"cmenergies":[],"observables":["CORR","ASYM","HELICITY"],"phrases":["Deep Inelastic Scattering","Strange production","Muon production","Asymmetry Measurement","Neutral Current","Inclusive"],"reactions":["MU+ DEUT --> MU+ K- X","MU+ DEUT --> MU+ PI+ X","MU+ DEUT --> MU+ PI- X","MU+ DEUT --> MU+ K+ X","MU+ DEUT --> MU+ X"]},"doc_type":"publication","doi":"10.1016/j.physletb.2009.08.065","first_author":{"affiliation":"Piemonte Orientale U., Alessandria","full_name":"Al